      "dom_id": "question-218599",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "If $f(x)=A\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{x}$ and $f(4)=2,$ then $A=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=4$ and $f(x)=2$ into the expression for $f(x)$ and solve for $A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =A\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{3})}^{4} \\\\ 2 & =A\\cdot (\\frac{{1}^{4}}{{3}^{4}}) \\\\ 2 & =A\\cdot \\frac{1}{81} \\\\ 2\\cdot 81 & =A \\\\ 162 & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A=162.$",
